gal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{W}","name":"Wall of Glare","oracle_id":"a59897cb-7ead-494a-a1d0-c9baf79bf18b","oracle_text":"Defender (This creature can't attack.)\nThis creature can block any number of creatures.","power":"0","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"1999-06-07","toughness":"5","type_line":"Creature — Wall"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Giggling Skitterspike is no longer on the battlefield when its second ability resolves, use its power as it last existed on the battlefield to determine how much damage it deals.","oracle_id":"ca02cb31-9850-48bf-bc8d-ed86a4d4d4f7","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Monstrous isn't an ability that a creature has. It's just something true about that creature. If the creature stops being a creature or loses its abilities, it will continue to be monstrous.","oracle_id":"ca02cb31-9850-48bf-bc8d-ed86a4d4d4f7","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once a creature becomes monstrous, it can't become monstrous again. If the creature is already monstrous when the monstrosity ability resolves, nothing happens.","oracle_id":"ca02cb31-9850-48bf-bc8d-ed86a4d4d4f7","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card now uses the Reach keyword ability to enable the blocking of flying creatures. This works because a creature with flying can only be blocked by creatures with flying or reach.","oracle_id":"e740ce2f-2134-473c-afa1-1b6d2d1e38ef","published_at":"2008-04-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
